 actually match.
 
+``merge_slashes`` is applied before comparing paths, so ``/a//b`` and ``/a/b``
+are duplicates. A trailing slash makes rules distinct (branch vs. leaf), so
+``/a`` and ``/a/`` are not duplicates regardless of ``strict_slashes``.
